  "markdown": "<!-- generated 2026-09-18T17:23:12Z by scheduled Claude task -->\n## Your roster: what changed this week\n- **Kyler Murray (bench, Questionable, concussion):** limited Wed and Thu, so he has a path to play, but independent clearance decides it. Backup Carson Wentz went 12-of-19, 133 yds, 3 TD in relief in Week 1 (Yahoo/Athlon, Sept 17-18). Nothing to do: he is not in your lineup. Jauan Jennings (bench, MIN WR) is fine either way, Wentz kept the offense moving. [Likely]\n- **Jakobi Meyers (bench, Questionable, thumb):** limited all camp and again this week, but played Week 1 (2 catches, 40 yds, TD) (RotoWire/First Coast News, Sept 2026). Plays at DEN. Keep on bench, he is not near your lineup anyway.\n- **Zach Charbonnet (IR, ACL):** PUP, surgery, no return this season. Consider it dead roster value; his IR spot is only useful if you need to stash someone.\n- **Lineup:** no starter carries an injury tag. No start/sit changes from news.\n\n## Waiver targets: news check\n- **Dallas Goedert (bid $25):** Week 1 was TE3 overall: 77 yds, 2 TD, 20% target share (SI/RotoBaller Week 2 columns, Sept 2026). Ignore the CBS \"ruled out for Week 2\" item: it is from Sept 12, 2025 (knee sprain, last year). No 2026 injury found. Red-zone role is real (11 of 13 career TDs inside the 20), but TD-driven weeks regress. Bid is reasonable; do not go higher than $25.\n- **Devin Singletary (bid $11) and Najee Harris (bid $10):** Same backfield, both behind Skattebo. Singletary scored in Week 1 (4 catches, 22 yds); Harris was a healthy scratch, and Tyrone Tracy fumbled and was benched, so the No. 3 spot is open (amNewYork, Sept 15; NBC Sports, Sept 8). Neither would start for you. Pick at most one, and Singletary is the safer one. Skip Harris: he is 3 games removed from an ACL and not active.\n- **Rest of the list (Turpin, Kelce, Johnson, Sadiq, Sanders):** no news pass done, all sub-$10 bids. [Guessing] Juwan Johnson is Questionable; skip unless he clears.\n\n## League: notab